On the IR obstacle part in the lab, the AO pin is connected to A0. The AO voltage rises in a straight line with proximity (a reading of about 51 for proximity 0 and about 972 for proximity 1). You set the proximity first to 0.4, then to 0.8. What do you see in the serial monitor?

```
void setup() {
  Serial.begin(9600);
}

void loop() {
  if (analogRead(A0) >= 600) Serial.println("Y");
  else Serial.println("N");
  delay(500);
}
```

You want to count the boxes on a conveyor belt. A single box stays in front of the sensor for one second and the counter goes up to 10 (it rises every 100 ms). Which line is the problem?

```
int sayac = 0;

void setup() {
  pinMode(3, INPUT);
  Serial.begin(9600);
}

void loop() {
  bool engel = (digitalRead(3) == LOW);
  if (engel) {
    sayac++;
    Serial.println(sayac);
  }
  delay(100);
}
```
